    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Challenges in Aerospace Chip Production</title>
      <p>Aerospace chip manufacturers face unique challenges in producing chips that must withstand extreme conditions, such as high altitudes, temperature fluctuations, and radiation exposure. The specialized nature of these chips requires rigorous testing and certification processes to ensure they perform reliably in mission-critical aerospace applications.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">The Future of Chips in Aerospace and Aviation</title>
      <p>The future of chips in aerospace and aviation lies in the development of even more efficient, durable, and high-performance components. As the industry embraces artificial intelligence, autonomous flight, and electric propulsion, chip technologies will continue to evolve to meet the increasing demands for speed, power, and efficiency in modern aircraft.</p>
